    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d352-a5">

                <pb facs="0625" n="497" xml:id="pg497"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 5 in No.
                    715.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The judge of instruction to
                        the commissary of the government</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Republic of Hayti</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#small-caps">Chamber of
                                Criminal Instruction</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-02-21"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 21,
                        1885</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Commissary</hi>: I acknowledge the receipt of
                    your letter of the 20th instant and the papers you have sent me in your
                    communication.</p>
                <p>I am upon the point of accomplishing the supplement of information which you have
                    required me to make. I hope to be able to finish next week.</p>
                <p>I salute you, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>ERNEST BONHOMME.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>P. S.—I return to you also the dispatches communicated.</p>
                    <p>A true copy.</p>
                    <p>The chief of bureau of the department of foreign relations,</p>
                    <closer><signed>M. DELVA.</signed></closer>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
